{% doc %}
  Renders an unbounded check-icon + text list in the product information column.

  Figma reference: 2013:19 / 2013:25 (desktop), 2013:66 (mobile).
  Column gap 16, per-row icon/text gap 10, rows top-aligned so wrapped text
  keeps the icon on the first line. Text is Body M/Regular 16 / 1.4 in #3F3F3F
  (a raw hex in the design — deliberately one shade off Neutral/700 #424242).

  Content comes from a single rich text block setting (`text`), which the
  merchant can also connect to a rich text metafield via a dynamic source.

  The rich text runs through the row splitter below: one row per bullet /
  paragraph / line break, whatever the editor produces. No separator character
  for the client to remember.

  The text supplies row TEXT ONLY. The icon comes from block settings and is the
  same for every row — `icon_type` picks image picker or pasted SVG, and the
  bundled check is the fallback. There is no per-row icon override.

  @param {object} block - Product section block settings and attributes.

  @example
  {% render 'pdp-highlight-list', block: block, product: product %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Rich text row splitting. Row breaks come from the MARKUP the rich text editor
    already emits — `</li>` (bullet or numbered list), `</p>` (enter = new
    paragraph), `<br>` (shift+enter) — all normalised to one internal delimiter
    before the split. The client never types a separator character; they press
    enter or click the bullet button.

    The delimiter is deliberately `||PDPROW||` rather than something typeable:
    any literal token would split rows when it appeared in real copy.

    `strip_html` runs AFTER the delimiters are injected, otherwise the block
    boundaries are gone and the whole field collapses into a single row. Inline
    formatting (bold, italic, links) is intentionally stripped — rows are plain
    text so the check-icon layout stays intact.
  endcomment
  assign richtext_items = ''
  assign richtext_count = 0
  assign richtext_html = block.settings.text

  if richtext_html != blank
    assign richtext_normalized = richtext_html
    assign richtext_normalized = richtext_normalized | replace: '</li>', '||PDPROW||'
    assign richtext_normalized = richtext_normalized | replace: '</p>', '||PDPROW||'
    assign richtext_normalized = richtext_normalized | replace: '<br>', '||PDPROW||'
    assign richtext_normalized = richtext_normalized | replace: '<br/>', '||PDPROW||'
    assign richtext_normalized = richtext_normalized | replace: '<br />', '||PDPROW||'
    assign richtext_normalized = richtext_normalized | strip_html
    assign richtext_items = richtext_normalized | split: '||PDPROW||'

    for richtext_text in richtext_items
      assign trimmed_richtext = richtext_text | strip
      if trimmed_richtext != blank
        assign richtext_count = richtext_count | plus: 1
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign render_source = 'none'
  if richtext_count > 0
    assign render_source = 'richtext'
  endif

  comment
    Empty content: hold the spot in the theme editor so the block stays
    findable and clickable, but emit nothing at all on preview links and live.
  endcomment
  assign show_block = false
  assign is_placeholder = false
  if render_source != 'none'
    assign show_block = true
  elsif request.design_mode
    assign show_block = true
    assign is_placeholder = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if show_block -%}
  {%- style -%}
    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} {
      padding-top: {{ block.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ block.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }

    /* Figma 2013:25 "Frame 745" — column, gap 16 */
    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} .pdp-highlight-list {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: {{ block.settings.row_gap }}px;
      width: 100%;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    /* Figma 2013:27 "Frame 740" — row, gap 10, align-items flex-start */
    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} .pdp-highlight-list__item {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: {{ block.settings.icon_gap }}px;
    }

    /* Figma 2013:28 "mingcute:check-fill" — 24x24 */
    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} .pdp-highlight-list__icon {
      width: {{ block.settings.icon_size }}px;
      height: {{ block.settings.icon_size }}px;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      display: block;
    }

    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} .pdp-highlight-list__icon svg {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      display: block;
    }

    /* Figma 2013:32 — Body M/Regular 16 / 1.4, #3F3F3F, wraps to fill the column */
    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} .pdp-highlight-list__text {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-width: 0;
      font-family: {{ block.settings.font_family }};
      font-size: {{ block.settings.font_size }};
      font-weight: {{ block.settings.font_weight }};
      line-height: {{ block.settings.line_height }};
      letter-spacing: 0;
      {%- if block.settings.text_color_mode == 'custom' %}
        color: {{ block.settings.color | default: '#3F3F3F' }};
      {%- endif %}
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} .pdp-highlight-list__text p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* Theme editor only — never reaches preview or live. */
    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} .pdp-highlight-list--placeholder .pdp-highlight-list__text {
      opacity: 0.5;
    }

    #pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }} .pdp-highlight-list__note {
      margin: 0 0 {{ block.settings.row_gap }}px;
      font-family: {{ block.settings.font_family }};
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      line-height: 1.4;
      color: #6B6B6B;
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    `icon_type` decides which icon setting is read; the other one is hidden in
    the editor, so falling back across them would resurrect a value the client
    can no longer see. The bundled check covers an empty pick either way.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture default_icon -%}
    {%- if block.settings.icon_type == 'image' and block.settings.icon_image != blank -%}
      {{-
        block.settings.icon_image
        | image_url: width: 96
        | image_tag: alt: '', widths: '24, 48, 96', loading: 'lazy'
      -}}
    {%- elsif block.settings.icon_type != 'image' and block.settings.icon != blank -%}
      {{- block.settings.icon -}}
    {%- else -%}
      {{- 'pdp-check.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  <div id="pdp-highlight-list-{{ block.id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- if is_placeholder -%}
      <p class="pdp-highlight-list__note">
        <strong>Highlight List — nothing to show yet.</strong>
        Type your list in the <em>Items</em> field in this block — press enter for each new row — or connect that field
        to a rich text metafield. This note and the sample rows below are visible only to you in the theme editor.
        Nothing at all is output on the live storefront while this block is empty.
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <ul
      class="pdp-highlight-list{% if is_placeholder %} pdp-highlight-list--placeholder{% endif %}"
      role="list"
    >
      {%- if is_placeholder -%}
        {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
          <li class="pdp-highlight-list__item">
            <span class="pdp-highlight-list__icon" aria-hidden="true">
              {{- default_icon -}}
            </span>
            <span class="pdp-highlight-list__text">Sample row {{ i }} — your text will replace this</span>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- elsif render_source == 'richtext' -%}
        {%- for item_text in richtext_items -%}
          {%- assign trimmed_text = item_text | strip -%}
          {%- if trimmed_text != blank -%}
            <li class="pdp-highlight-list__item">
              <span class="pdp-highlight-list__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                {{- default_icon -}}
              </span>
              <span class="pdp-highlight-list__text">{{ trimmed_text }}</span>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
